/-!
# The morphism of a linear system to `ℙⁿ_k`: finiteness, closed immersion, and the plane conic

Let `k` be a field, `X` a proper integral scheme of dimension one over `k`, `ℒ` an invertible
`𝒪_X`-module and `s₀, …, sₙ` global sections of `ℒ` generating it. The morphism
`φ = Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio.toPolynomialModel s hs f : X ⟶ Proj k[T₀, …, Tₙ]` of
[Stacks, Tag 01NE] is, on the chart `X_{sᵢ}`, the morphism of the ratios `sⱼ / sᵢ`. This file
proves what the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0C6N] (and part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0C6T]) needs from it:

* `φ⁻¹(D₊(Tᵢ)) = X_{sᵢ}`;
* `φ` is finite as soon as no `sᵢ` is nowhere vanishing — it is proper, and a fibre is either a
  finite set of closed points or, if it meets the generic point and a closed point, all of `X`,
  which would put `X` inside one chart — so the charts `X_{sᵢ}` are affine;
* `φ` is a closed immersion as soon as on every chart the functions are generated by the constants
  and the ratios (or on two charts covering `X`), and then `ℒ` is very ample relative to `f`;
* for three `k`-linearly independent sections on a genus-zero curve the image is a plane curve
  whose equation has degree `2`: degree `1` would make a linear form in the sections vanish, and
  genus zero rules out degree at least `3` by [Stacks, Tag 0BYD].

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.PlaneConic.preimage_basicOpen_toPolynomialModel`: the preimage of `D₊(Tᵢ)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.PlaneConic.isFinite_toPolynomialModel` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.PlaneConic.isAffineOpen_nvCover`: finiteness, and affineness of the charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.PlaneConic.isClosedImmersion_toPolynomialModel`: the closed immersion, from
  generation on every chart; `isClosedImmersion_toPolynomialModel_of_sup` from two charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.PlaneConic.isRelativelyVeryAmple_of_isClosedImmersion_toPolynomialModel`:
  a closed immersion `φ` makes `ℒ` very ample relative to `f`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.PlaneConic.exists_planeCurveData_deg_two`: the plane conic.

## Implementation notes

The chart computations are the library's: the pullback of `Tⱼ / Tᵢ` along `φ` is the ratio
(`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio.appLE_coordFracAt_chart`) and the pullback of a constant is the
constant (`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio.appLE_coeffToAway_chart`). Very ampleness passes
through the base-change model `ℙⁿ_{Spec k}`, of which the polynomial model is an isomorphic copy:
the pinned twist comparison
`Stacks.TwistPullbackPinned.exists_iso_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse` identifies `ℒ` with
`φ^* 𝒪(1)`, which is [Stacks, Tag 01VS]'s per-degree conclusion, and
`Stacks.AmpleRelativeFiniteType.isRelativelyVeryAmple_of_hasImmersionTwistOver` turns it into
[Stacks, Tag 01VM] very ampleness over the affine base `Spec k`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C6N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C6T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BYB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BYB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BYD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BYD)
-/

